#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186310633 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3146eb6-b4ef-554d-83c1-351a3fb15651" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the First Terms of the Taylor Series of a Function About a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4d424f9-994f-5e5f-8a16-d0e21575bdd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310635} {:answer/id #uuid "bb6ac4dc-fc04-54e5-9bb8-5e2b2fc3524c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310636}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb6ac4dc-fc04-54e5-9bb8-5e2b2fc3524c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310636} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e91e638-9a0f-5257-bdcb-466b2c7df9c5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310634} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d1e6ce05-f3ac-5192-a716-ebfbf206cc8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310638}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1e6ce05-f3ac-5192-a716-ebfbf206cc8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310638} :answer-field/id #uuid "83c01ef3-bb1d-5089-893f-524c6e531279" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310637} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6bf25ab4-42e5-5454-88ac-5de4f783d11f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310640}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6bf25ab4-42e5-5454-88ac-5de4f783d11f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310640} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5960653-e1a0-5b43-a7a5-33a593a2293f" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310639}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "98ed4bd4-cd51-5bf7-857e-4a26fd6e986f" :question/math-academy-id "q-353917" :question/problem "Find the first three non-zero terms in the Taylor expansion of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ centered about the point $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\n$\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=$\n{{field-1}}\n$+$\n{{field-2}}\n${(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}\\,-\\,$\n{{field-3}}\n${(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{4}\\,+⋯$" :question/worked-solution "We use Taylor's formula in the form\n\n$$\nf(x)=f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(a)}{2!}(x-a)^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{‴}(a)}{3!}(x-a)^{3}+⋯,\n$$\n\nwith $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $a=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ \n\nComputing the required derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ f\\,(-\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =sin\\,(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})=-1 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{′}\\,(-\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =cos\\,(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})=0 \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{″}\\,(-\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =-sin\\,(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})=1 \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{‴}\\,(-\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =-cos\\,(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})=0 \\\\ {f}^{(4)}(x) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{(4)}\\,(-\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =sin\\,(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})=-1. \\\\ \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =-1+0\\,(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\frac{1}{2!}\\,{(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}+\\frac{0}{3!}\\,{(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{3}+\\frac{(-1)}{4!}\\,{(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{4}+⋯ \\\\  & =-1+\\frac{1}{2}\\,{(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}-\\frac{1}{24}\\,{(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{4}+⋯.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
